  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nSaturday is forecasted to see the hottest temperatures of the \nweek, but dense smoke may persist and continue to slightly \nmoderate peak temperatures. A stalled upper low over British \nColumbia will begin to move inland through Saturday and is set \nto bring a dry cold front through the area Saturday evening into\nSunday. With Saturday being the hottest day, this combination \nof heat, very dry conditions, and frontal gusty winds will lead \nto critical fire weather conditions across the area. Behind the \ncold front, Sunday through Monday will be 5-10 degrees cooler \nthan normal, but dry and gusty conditions will remain, leading \nto continued elevated fire weather conditions. Temperatures \nbegin to climb again Tuesday and Wednesday as a Pacific high \npressure system builds into the West Coast and Desert Southwest.\nWarm and dry conditions will remain through midweek in the \nextended period.",
